    "reasoning": "Each field agrees with its own captured worked solution and the earlier individual review. q-317356: the graph increases toward y=1 from below and has intercept (0,-2); current option 3 is equivalent to the solution's final annotated graph. q-84980: ordered words without repetition number 5·4·3=60. q-122216: P(6,3)=6!/3!=120. q-28338: the original slope is -2/5, whose negative reciprocal is 5/2. q-47943: the quotient rule gives e^x(cos x+sin x)/cos²x. q-48507: the derivative (x cos x-sin x)/(2x²) evaluates to -1/(2π). q-110536: taking logarithms of e^(y+1)=4 gives y=2 ln(2)-1. q-134008 and q-134009: the plotted patterns are curved; 'no linear trend' here means no adequate approximately straight relationship, rather than no association. q-134023: (2,2) and (7,8) give slope 6/5 and intercept -2/5. q-134019: (0,9) and (7,3) give slope -6/7 and intercept 9. q-134031: an estimated line through (2,5) and (6,1) gives y=-x+7. q-133768: an estimated line through (2,2) and (6,8) has slope 1.5. These estimates already meet the requested rounding. q-51317: the source specifies base-10 logarithms, giving derivative -1/((1-x)ln(10)). q-6913: cancellation leaves 1/(x²+2) for x≠0, so zero is a removable hole and there are no vertical asymptotes. q-31283: differentiating -6 csc x gives +6 csc x cot x; the current choice uses the source's plain function formatting. Confirmation is based on worked solutions, not revealed grades.",
